  <data name="EachAlarmIsCheckedNote" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Each alarm is checked on its own interval, so the loop only touches the database when one is actually due. An alarm announces only what it has not announced before — a condition that stays true does not repeat itself — which is why a check that keeps matching shows here as armed rather than as firing over and over.</value>
    <comment>Note in BackgroundProcessesView.</comment>
  </data>
